# Frontend: Next.js 16 and React 19

`{{ fp }}app/`: routes (App Router); `{{ fp }}components/`: components; `{{ fp }}lib/`: API
client and constants (`constants.ts`). Read `{{ fp }}AGENTS.md` before using a Next.js API.
Run: `kiln dev`; check: `kiln check` (ESLint, `tsc`).

## Code

- **[STRICT-TS]** Strict TypeScript in every `.ts` and `.tsx`.
- **[NO-ANY]** No `any`: `unknown`, then a type narrowing (ESLint rule).
- **[ASYNC-AWAIT]** `async/await` with `try/catch` only; `.then().catch()` chains are banned.
- **[MODERN-REACT]** React 19 / Next.js 16 (App Router): actions for mutations, `use()` and
  `Suspense` for asynchronous code. Never a class component, never `useEffect` to load data.
- **[SERVER-FIRST]** Server components by default. `"use client"` only for a component that
  handles an interaction (state, event, browser API), as low as possible in the tree: a whole
  page is never a client component.
- **[EXPLICIT-IMPORTS]** Imports through the `@/` alias (`@/components/…`, `@/lib/…`), never a
  relative path that climbs (`../../`).
- **[API-CALLS]** Components never call the API directly: they go through a typed function of
  `lib/` (`lib/api.ts`) that validates the response before returning it.
- **[MUTATIONS]** A write goes through a server action (`"use server"`) that validates its
  inputs, never through a `fetch` written in a client component.
- **[UI-STATES]** Every screen that loads data handles the three states explicitly: loading
  (`Suspense` or `loading.tsx`), error (`error.tsx`, an understandable message, never "Error."
  alone) and empty list.
- **[ACCESSIBILITY]** Every field has an associated `<label>`, every icon button an `aria-label`,
  every informative image an `alt` (`next/image`). Everything works with the keyboard and focus
  stays visible.
- **[TEST-DENSITY]** The front's test density never drops: its floor in `charter.toml` is raised
  as it goes up (floor).

## Styling

- **[STYLE-1]** No CSS Modules nor inline {% raw %}`style={{ }}`{% endraw %}: Tailwind in `className`.
- **[STYLE-2]** **Tailwind by default**, right in the JSX. Separate CSS only for a multi-step
  animation, a native browser element or a black-box third-party component.
- **[STYLE-3]** `app/globals.css` is the only CSS file: it imports Tailwind and holds the theme
  tokens (`@theme`). A component writes the class of a token, never an arbitrary value that
  copies it (`text-[0.7rem]`).
- **[STYLE-5]** Banned: bursts of arbitrary classes, `@apply` to rebuild a component (that is a
  React component's job), `!important` except to override a third-party library that forces it.
{%- if level >= 2 %}

## Performance and quality

- **[CORE-WEB-VITALS]** Budgets at the 75th percentile, on mobile: **LCP < 2.5 s**,
  **INP < 200 ms**, **CLS < 0.1**. A regression beyond them blocks the release.
- **[JS-BUDGET]** A JavaScript budget per page, checked at build time; every heavy library is
  loaded on demand (`next/dynamic`).
- **[MODERN-IMAGES]** Images through `next/image`, in AVIF/WebP, sized, loaded lazily below the
  first screen.
- **[E2E-JOURNEYS]** Critical journeys have a Playwright end-to-end test, run in CI against a full
  stack.
- **[AUTOMATED-ACCESSIBILITY]** Main pages pass an automated `axe-core` check; target
  **WCAG 2.2 level AA**.
